{"name":"Bolognese","hex":"#bb4400","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bolognese","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, from or relating to the city of Bologna, capital and largest city of Emilia-Romagna, Italy, or the surrounding metropolitan city.","Of a pasta sauce, made from minced veal, pork and beef, onions, garlic, tomato, bay leaf, carrot and celery and wine."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native or inhabitant of the city of Bologna, capital and largest city of Emilia-Romagna, Italy, or the surrounding metropolitan city.","A dog of a small breed of the bichon type, originating in Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bolognese"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bologna","blocks":[{"text":"Bologna is the capital and largest city of the Emilia-Romagna region in northern Italy. It is the seventh most populous city in Italy, with 391,473 inhabitants from 150 different nationalities. Its metropolitan province is home to more than 1 million people as of 2026. Bologna is most famous for being the home to the oldest university in continuous operation, the University of Bologna, established in AD 1088."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Torri_di_Bologna%2C_Bologna.jpg/330px-Torri_di_Bologna%2C_Bologna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bologna","wikidata":"Q1891"},{"title":"Bolognese sauce","blocks":[{"text":"Bolognese sauce, known in Italian as ragù alla bolognese or ragù bolognese, is the main variety of ragù in Italian cuisine, typical of the city of Bologna."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Tagliatelle_al_rag%C3%B9_%28image_modified%29.jpg/330px-Tagliatelle_al_rag%C3%B9_%28image_modified%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolognese_sauce","wikidata":"Q1162965"},{"title":"Bolognese (dog breed)"